codex
For Task 1, I’m using the production encoder itself, not a hand-written vector: two admissible network descriptions share one sealed `ActionEvaluation`, while only omitted background outcomes/coupled-power results change. The exact targets are then produced by `targets.py`. This makes byte equality executable and keeps label arithmetic independent of the encoder.

For Task 3, the existing 176,223-row pilot artifact contains proxy labels, so I will not treat them as exact. I’ll reuse its actual Q1/Q2 rows and action identities, replay a bounded set of those singleton actions through the exact evaluator, and group-hold out whole anchors. The comparison will use the same standardized k-nearest-neighbor regressor for Q-only and Q-plus-discarded outcome structure, with tuning confined to training anchors.
